{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-211038",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Dividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.\n\nThe reciprocal of $10$ is $\\frac{1}{10}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\,÷\\,10=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\times \\,\\frac{1}{10}.\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\times \\frac{1}{10}=\\frac{1\\times 1}{2\\times 10}=\\frac{1}{20}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
